    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213-a3">

                <pb facs="0396" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg296"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 594.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr.
                            Fouchard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch of the 13th instant with its inclosure.</p>
                <p>You will permit me, Mr. Minister, in acknowledging the receipt of such dispatch,
                    to state that the rights of any American citizens who may be found in either
                    Jacmel or Jérémie, when your Government shall attempt the bombardment of such
                    cities, according to the address of the President transmitted, as inclosed in
                    your dispatch, as well as according to the terms of the dispatch itself, are
                    distinctly and specially reserved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
